Patch to upstream OpenCV: initialize the chart type of mcc::CCheckerDetector.

CCheckerDetectorImpl declares `ColorChart m_chartType;` without an initializer, and its
constructor is empty. When the MCC module moved from opencv_contrib into objdetect for
5.0, the chart type stopped being a process() argument and became a member set through
setColorChartType(), but nothing sets it before that call. A detector used without
setColorChartType() therefore reads whatever was left on the heap: measured on this
build, the first detector created in a process reported a chart type that is not a valid
ColorChart value and detected nothing, while later ones happened to reuse memory that
held 0 and worked — the same image gave different results depending on what had been
allocated before.

The fix initializes it to MCC24, the first enumerator, which is what callers that never
set it expect. test/unit/mcc.test.js detects a chart with a freshly created detector.

Applied by build/build.sh after cloning the source; a patch that no longer applies fails
the build instead of silently producing an unpatched artifact.

--- a/modules/objdetect/src/mcc/checker_detector.hpp
+++ b/modules/objdetect/src/mcc/checker_detector.hpp
@@ -176,7 +176,7 @@ protected:
     bool m_useDnn = false;
 #endif
     DetectorParametersMCC m_params = DetectorParametersMCC();
-    ColorChart m_chartType;
+    ColorChart m_chartType = MCC24;

 private: // methods aux
     void get_subbox_chart_physical(
